From 8f8287896293a431b81e1f3252af1af3b7d71714 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lab <lab@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 06:34:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] LAB: release the detector flow at window end or handoff;
 log refused admissions; host_mismatch (SEC-CULV-1, SEC-CULV-2)

SEC-CULV-1 (P2): the engine flow, its admission slot and its 32 KiB
reservation were held until the tunnel closed, so 4,096 idle tunnels
exhausted admission and every later tunnel went unobserved with no
record. The flow is now finished when the observation window ends (the
timer: Expire, then Finish) or when both directions have left
observation (handoff or end), whichever is first. Its record is kept
and logged at tunnel close with the forwarded bytes. A refused admission
relays unobserved and logs a record with admission "refused" and
reason admission_refused. The fake engine now reports a finished flow
as done, as the real engine's closed flow is.

SEC-CULV-2 (P3): host_mismatch, the client-asserted host against the
CONNECT destination compared port-normalised (52eb9d1's labSignals), is
computed on the unredacted record before the hostnames are pseudonymized,
and logged as a categorical signal.

Tests (protodetect_lab_test.go): window end and handoff each release
admission while the tunnel stays open; refused admission is logged;
host_mismatch survives redaction and leaks no host; host normalisation
table. 20 runs under -race. Both SEC-CULV-1 tests fail with the release
removed, and the SEC-CULV-2 test fails with the comparison moved after
redaction.

